Spawn module: src/amk/amk_spawn.c holds the slots, mail and its drain, the fork, the process
groups and the terminal, the deferred call, the wait, and the sweep at exit. This patch is
make's side of the move: the moved code leaves main.c and the object joins the build.

amk_run_goals stays in main.c, since it is the bridge to make's own goal handling, and it
and amk_rearm_pid lose static so a spawned job reaches them. The served child's connection,
amk_conn, loses static so the fork can close it, and the forward declaration of the mail
pipe goes, since the module now defines it.

